                            <comment id="15353491" author="vladisav" created="Tue, 28 Jun 2016 18:26:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Denis,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;are you sure this is a bug? &lt;br/&gt;
I think if there is no backup configured (which is default in AtomicConfiguration?), failure is unavoidable.&lt;br/&gt;
See &lt;a href=&quot;http://mail-archives.apache.org/mod_mbox/ignite-dev/201604.mbox/%3CCAGcMBHjYdtMtwpB7fGAjSG7g2evohNkNKtpvOW5LDP8+o5paXA@mail.gmail.com%3E&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;this thread&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15355111" author="dmagda" created="Wed, 29 Jun 2016 12:09:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Vladislav,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is definitely the bug because &lt;tt&gt;lock.await&lt;/tt&gt; mustn&apos;t hang if the node that stored the lock left topology and there are no backups left. In this scenario after the exception that is in the description occurs the node, where it&apos;s happened and which tries to acquire the lock, silently hanging at  &lt;tt&gt;lock.await&lt;/tt&gt; method.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15393800" author="vladisav" created="Tue, 26 Jul 2016 13:40:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Denis,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I agree, this sounds like a bug; but it seems I can&apos;t reproduce it myself. Could you please make a test, like one in GridCacheAbstractDataStructuresFailoverSelfTest? The following addition to your scenario does throw the exception you wrote:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;4) Start third node&lt;br/&gt;
5) Stop second node&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(third node gets exception, if no backups are set) Is this what you meant? But I still can&apos;t make the node hang.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15405038" author="dmagda" created="Tue, 2 Aug 2016 23:49:04 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Vladislav,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I was wrong, there is no hanging happens when the exception, discussed in the ticket, is thrown. I&apos;ve improved the test (LockIssueVer2.java) and now the exception is 100% reproducible.  In my understanding we should catch this exception internally and re-create the lock from scratch if &lt;tt&gt;create=true&lt;/tt&gt; flag is set to &lt;tt&gt;true&lt;/tt&gt;. What do you think?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15532461" author="saikiran939" created="Thu, 29 Sep 2016 10:57:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;we are seeing this issue too when we acquire a lock after the node has left the cluster. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;any fix planned ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15842614" author="ezhuravl" created="Fri, 27 Jan 2017 11:52:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi Vladislav,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Can you confirm that you are still working on the issue. I am also interested in this functionality and would like to give it a go if you are no longer working on it.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15887632" author="ezhuravl" created="Tue, 28 Feb 2017 09:16:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Done, tc link: &lt;a href=&quot;http://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=IgniteTests&amp;amp;tab=projectOverview&amp;amp;branch_IgniteTests=pull%2F1578%2Fmerge&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=IgniteTests&amp;amp;tab=projectOverview&amp;amp;branch_IgniteTests=pull%2F1578%2Fmerge&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;br/&gt;
pull request: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1578&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/1578&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15892145" author="vladisav" created="Thu, 2 Mar 2017 12:26:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Good job, thank you for the contribution, sorry for delayed response. I made some minor comments in PR. &lt;br/&gt;
What happens if failoverSafe == false? I&apos;m thinking, if user opted for lock that explicitly throws exceptions if something goes wrong, do we need to somehow inform him that new state has been created? What do you think?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15892192" author="ezhuravl" created="Thu, 2 Mar 2017 12:53:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Vladislav, thanks for comments in PR, I added some minor corrections. Also, I think it&apos;s a good idea to log when new state for lock is created.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15892238" author="vladisav" created="Thu, 2 Mar 2017 13:29:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Great! Another remark - what happens with nodes awaiting on lock conditions once the lock is recreated? Will they remain blocked? Can you make a test for this also?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15892308" author="ezhuravl" created="Thu, 2 Mar 2017 14:13:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I already added it, you could check GridCacheWorkAfterRecreateLockTest&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15924208" author="ezhuravl" created="Tue, 14 Mar 2017 13:43:16 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://apache-ignite-developers.2346864.n4.nabble.com/IgniteSemaphore-and-failoverSafe-flag-td11945.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://apache-ignite-developers.2346864.n4.nabble.com/IgniteSemaphore-and-failoverSafe-flag-td11945.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
